        "worked_solution": "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=⟨0,1,1⟩.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =⟨-3,2,4⟩-⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $c=⟨1,1,1⟩$ of the point $C,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\ r & =⟨1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,1,1⟩+t⟨-4,1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
