        "math_academy_id": "q-149736",
        "knowledge_point_id": "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba",
        "knowledge_point": "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules",
        "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}=20.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+3) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}({b}_{j}+3) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}3) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}{b}_{j}+3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{15}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (20+3\\cdot 15) \\\\  & =(35-30)\\cdot (20+45) \\\\  & =(5)\\cdot (65) \\\\  & =325.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
